&lt;p&gt;I don&#8217;t see a significant difference when using max_rpcs_in_flight=8 and max_mod_rpcs_in_flight=8 in the 8 MDT case.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In any case, file creation scaling with the number of processes is now close to that of both unique directory and shared directory operations. (e.g. mdtest-hard)&lt;br/&gt;
I think this will help a lot for IO500 on small clusters (e.g., 10 nodes), where we previously needed many mount points (import/export) to saturate metadata performance when the system has many MDTs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We used to rely on multiple mount points for this, which is allowed and represents a real use case (e.g., Docker containers or sub-directory mounts on a single client). However, above results demonstrated that we can now achieve similar performance even with a single mount point.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
